builtin_fixture — Scale the absolute value of a number                       core · tier 0 · since 0.5.0 · 1.0 · exact

USAGE
    builtin_fixture(x, scale: Float = _two())

DESCRIPTION
    The absolute value of `x`, as `abs` gives it, times `scale`. Given a column, it applies to every row in
    one pass, through the lifted operators of its body.

ARGUMENTS
    x           Float. The number, or a column of numbers.
    scale:      Float = _two(). The factor; 2 unless given.

VALUE
    `abs(x) * scale`, a Float; a column of Floats when `x` is a column.

WARNINGS AND NOTES
    Z0211   an Int result does not fit in 64 bits

ACCURACY
    Exact.

SEE ALSO
    abs, sign

EXAMPLES
    > builtin_fixture(-3)
    6
    > builtin_fixture(1.5, scale: 3)
    4.5
